  "notes": "Compound of {密|みつ} (secret) + {輸|ゆ} (transport). Functions as a する verb ({密輸|みつゆ}する = to smuggle).\n\nUSAGE:\nCommonly encountered in news reporting about illegal trade. The verb form {密輸|みつゆ}する means \"to smuggle.\" The person who smuggles is {密輸|みつゆ}{業者|ぎょうしゃ} (smuggler) or {密輸|みつゆ}{犯|はん} (smuggling offender).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {密輸|みつゆ}する — to smuggle\n- {密輸|みつゆ}{品|ひん} — smuggled goods, contraband\n- {密輸|みつゆ}{業者|ぎょうしゃ} — smuggler\n- {密輸|みつゆ}ルート — smuggling route\n- {武器|ぶき}の{密輸|みつゆ} — arms smuggling\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {密売|みつばい} — illegal sale, black market dealing (selling, not transporting)\n- {密入国|みつにゅうこく} — illegal entry into a country (people, not goods)\n- {闇取引|やみとりひき} — black market transaction (broader, includes domestic illegal trade)",
